# DM26-0670
# infra/load-plans/slow-sink.nuon
#
# A sink that falls behind (docs/architecture/cassini-backpressure.md, "Tests, first"): one producer as fast as its
# window allows, one sink spending 0, 50 or 500 microseconds on each message, at 64 KiB and 1 MiB. The broker's
# memory is in every record (broker_usage); acceptance: its peak stays within its budget (half its container's memory
# limit by default) plus a fixed overhead, and nothing is lost below the stall bound. 6 runs.
#
# Until acknowledgements are the domain's, the sink's client acknowledges a delivery when it hands it to the sink, so
# a slow sink's backlog waits in the sink's mailbox, not the broker (cassini-backpressure.md, "As built"); the
# broker's side of a slow reader is what cassini/broker/tests/backpressure.rs tests. To measure under other bounds, add
# `broker: { CASSINI_MEMORY_BUDGET_BYTES: [...], CASSINI_STALL_SECS: [...] }` (with Flux's polar-agents suspended).
#
#   nu infra/load-harness.nu run infra/load-plans/slow-sink.nuon
{
  name: "slow-sink"
  defaults: { seconds: 20, max_count: 20000, max_bytes: 1073741824, warmup: 100, rate: 0 }
  grid: {
    size: [65536 1048576]
    sink_delay_us: [0 50 500]
    shape: [
      { producers: 1, sinks: 1, lanes: 1 }
    ]
  }
}
